-- The chord generator: a chord rhythm and a progression written across the chord pattern.
-- Hand-written: edit this file. Only the PRESETS block is filled in by tools/build.py (from its PRE lists and PROGS),
-- so the presets live in one place.
--
-- [ockm-chordmaker <track>] listens to:
--   ockm-<track>-rhythm   which chord rhythm (CHORD_RHYTHMS)
--   ockm-<track>-prog     which progression (PROGRESSIONS)
--   ockm-<track>-rate     how fast the chords change: 0 every half bar, 1 every bar, 2 every two bars
--   ockm-<track>-push     1: every chord change lands an eighth (two steps) early
--   ockm-<track>-gen      rebuild now
--   ockm-<track>-len      the pattern's length in steps (on auto, a new length rebuilds to fill it)
--   ockm-<track>-mode     0 auto (made for you), 1 edited by hand
--   ockm-loading          1 while a project loads (nothing rebuilds then)
-- and writes ockm-pat-<track>-on (0 rest, 1 hit, 2 accent) and ockm-pat-<track>-deg (the chord's root, a scale step),
-- then sends ockm-chord-changed. Any change to rhythm, progression, rate or push puts the part back on auto.
-- The bass reads the same deg table, so it follows the chords (and their push).

local cm = pd.Class:new():register("ockm-chordmaker")

